<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75775" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ πω,</span></b>  Conj. and Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>and not yet, not as yet</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				322
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				172c
			</span></i>, etc.: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, mostly with a word between, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέ
				τί πω, οὐδ᾽ ἄν πω</span>, etc., always of the past (cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔπω</span>): later with
			pres., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				106b
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σὺ δὲ οὐδέπω ὁρᾷς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			: with fut., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσον οὐδέπω συμβήσεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zos.
					2.1
				</span></i>
			; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδέποτε</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
